    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing and Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling — MorphoEval overall 93.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py` (overall weighted score: 93.1/100, up from 53.6/100 in v1). The remediated script computes exact Euclidean Distance Transform Largest Empty Circle radii R_LEC(A) and outer periclinal wall stresses across cell area A in [250, 4500] um^2 (WT R_LEC plateau 11.576 um vs ref 11.4 um; scaling r = 0.9859, p = 2.97e-4, RMSE = 0.314 um; 3.27x stress reduction vs unlobed isotropic cells); integrates a 196-node coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 cortical reaction-diffusion PDE system across shared anticlinal walls (intracortical r = -0.9899, trans-wall complementarity r = 0.9998, wavelength 24.50 um vs ref 24.5 um); validates ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutant lobeyness collapse (ktn1 L = 1.1107 vs ref 1.11, WT S = 0.6735 vs ref 0.68); and segments 10 interlocking puzzle cells on the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis leaf epidermis SEM micrograph (`arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg`, mean S = 0.720). Overall 93.0/100 (faithfulness 92.6, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/pavement_cell_lobing_comparison.png: rendered output of 2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py at 8871db0, image/png, 961496 B, 2548×1568 px, artifact_sha256 8df82fae6327068a70bf77aefe4e8d85e05dc9e0d53c002655ab4d6165803e01 (sha256 8df82fae6327068a70bf77aefe4e8d85e05dc9e0d53c002655ab4d6165803e01), spec_fingerprint 972460a5749d7d30868f5de9c61bcfd278fa143f89d629090a75b7aa4ebdc287. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 972460a5749d7d30868f5de9c61bcfd278fa143f89d629090a75b7aa4ebdc287; artifact_sha256: 8df82fae6327068a70bf77aefe4e8d85e05dc9e0d53c002655ab4d6165803e01; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg=4b7c1062f6ebfd6e..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/paper_citations.bib=e5d0ea8ec26365c9..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/pavement_cell_lobing_reference.json=de4e6daab5eae4a0..., datasets/pavement_cell_lobing/scout_manifest.json=72c917ec10ac1a55...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794 outer periclinal cell wall tensile stress scaling with Largest Empty Circle radius (sigma_max ~ P * R_LEC / h), demonstrating that interdigitated puzzle lobing pins R_LEC near ~11.4 um as cell area expands to 4500 um^2 whereas isotropic polygonal/mutant cells grow as sqrt(A/pi) | Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120:687-700 & Lin et al. (2013) Curr Biol 23:290-297 antagonistic cortical ROP2-RIC4 (actin lobe outgrowth) and ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 (katanin-mediated microtubule neck bundling) polarization in antiphase across shared anticlinal cell walls, and lobeyness collapse in rop2 rop4 RNAi and ktn1/ric1 mutants; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2D Euclidean Distance Transform Largest Empty Circle (R_LEC) and ConvexHull solidity/lobeyness solver across cell area growth A in [250, 4500] um^2 for wild-type Col-0 puzzle cells, unlobed isotropic cells, ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutants, and parallel-file monocot epidermis | 196-node periodic anticlinal boundary coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 reaction-diffusion PDE integrator reproducing intracortical mutual exclusion (r = -0.9899), trans-wall lobe-neck complementarity (r = 0.9998), 24.5 um lobe wavelength, and exact intercellular area conservation | Automated DoG + zero-compactness watershed segmentation of 10 interlocking puzzle-shaped pavement cells from the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana leaf epidermis SEM micrograph (`arabidopsis_pavement_cell_specimen.jpg`, mean S = 0.720, min S = 0.626, mean L = 1.506); transfer_boundary: 2D anticlinal boundary PDE and spring-remodeled polygonal contours with Euclidean Distance Transform R_LEC mapped to 2D epidermal SEM projections; does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-element shell modeling of dome deflection z(x,y) coupled to discrete microtubule filament polymerization stochastics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D spring-remodeling pavement cell polygon network to a 3D pressurized periclinal shell finite-element solver to resolve out-of-plane anticlinal wall buckling variations with depth." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
