<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) Largest Empty Circle (LEC) Turgor Stress Suppression Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that puzzle-shaped interdigitation pins the Largest Empty Circle radius R_LEC near the neck half-width R_0 (~11 um) as cell area A grows 10-20x, suppressing outer periclinal wall tensile stress by >3x compared to unlobed isotropic cells | Variables: P: turgor pressure (MPa); h: outer periclinal cell wall thickness (um); R_LEC: radius of Largest Empty/Inscribed Circle inside cell contour (um); R_0: bounded neck half-width (um); N = A/(π R_0^2): effective lobe-unit area multiple" ;
    dct:source "Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794 Figs. 1-3 & Box 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L95-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_039_pavement_cell_lobing.lean#L31-L50> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def puzzle_lec_radius_sq (r0_sq : Int) : Int := r0_sq
def isotropic_radius_sq (N r0_sq : Int) : Int := N * r0_sq
theorem sapala_2018_lec_stress_suppression (N r0_sq : Int)
    (hN : N ≥ 2) (hr0 : r0_sq > 0) :
    isotropic_radius_sq N r0_sq - puzzle_lec_radius_sq r0_sq = (N - 1) * r0_sq ∧
    2 * puzzle_lec_radius_sq r0_sq ≤ isotropic_radius_sq N r0_sq ∧
    puzzle_lec_radius_sq r0_sq < isotropic_radius_sq N r0_sq
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_max = P R_LEC / (2h);  R_LEC^2(WT) = R_0^2 ≪ R_iso^2(A) = A / π = N R_0^2  (for N ≥ 2 lobes)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.01.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-019-0500-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.32794> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled ROP2–ROP6 Cross-Inhibitory Cortical Reaction–Diffusion, Turgor-Driven Largest Empty Circle (LEC) Stress Scaling & Sinusoidal Anticlinal Wall Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.puzzle_lec_radius_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.sapala_2018_lec_stress_suppression" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Fu et al. (2005) ROP2–ROP6 Trans-Wall Complementarity & Intercellular Area Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes alternating ROP2 (convex lobe outgrowth) and ROP6 (concave neck microtubule bundling) domains in antiphase across shared anticlinal walls while preserving contiguous epidermal tiling without intercellular gaps | Variables: U(s,t): active cortical ROP2-RIC4 concentration; V(s,t): active cortical ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 concentration; V_opp: opposing cell cortical ROP6 across shared anticlinal wall; δ_lobe: local anticlinal wall displacement" ;
    dct:source "Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120(5):687-700 Figs. 1-7; Bidhendi et al. (2019) Nature Plants 5:981-992" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L220-L355>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_039_pavement_cell_lobing.lean#L68-L83> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cell_A_lobe_area (A0 d_lobe : Int) : Int := A0 + d_lobe
def cell_B_neck_area (B0 d_lobe : Int) : Int := B0 - d_lobe
def cortical_rop_polarity (rop2 rop6 : Int) : Int := rop2 - rop6
theorem fu_2005_rop2_rop6_trans_wall_conservation (A0 B0 d_lobe r_hi r_lo : Int) :
    cell_A_lobe_area A0 d_lobe + cell_B_neck_area B0 d_lobe = A0 + B0 ∧
    cortical_rop_polarity r_hi r_lo + cortical_rop_polarity r_lo r_hi = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂U/∂t = D_u ∂²U/∂s² + (k_0 + k_a U²/(1+U²))/(1 + γ_{26} V²) (1 + α V_opp) - k_off U;  A_A(δ) + A_B(-δ) = A_0 + B_0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.01.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-019-0500-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.32794> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled ROP2–ROP6 Cross-Inhibitory Cortical Reaction–Diffusion, Turgor-Driven Largest Empty Circle (LEC) Stress Scaling & Sinusoidal Anticlinal Wall Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.cell_A_lobe_area" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.fu_2005_rop2_rop6_trans_wall_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Lin et al. (2013) ktn1 / rop2 rop4 Mutant Lobeyness & Solidity Collapse Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that loss of ROP2/ROP4 or katanin KTN1/RIC1 microtubule severing collapses lobeyness to L -> 1 and solidity to S -> 1, causing unchecked R_LEC ~ sqrt(A/pi) growth and high periclinal wall tensile stress | Variables: L = P_perim / P_hull: pavement cell lobeyness; S = A_cell / A_hull: convex solidity; k_rop: ROP2-ROP6-KTN1 mechanochemical coupling strength; A_lobe: sinusoidal lobe amplitude" ;
    dct:source "Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794 Fig. 5; Lin et al. (2013) Current Biology 23:290-297" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L360-L470>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_039_pavement_cell_lobing.lean#L99-L115> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lobed_perimeter (P_hull k_rop A_lobe : Int) : Int := P_hull + k_rop * A_lobe
def lobed_hull_area (A_cell k_rop A_indent : Int) : Int := A_cell + k_rop * A_indent
theorem sapala_2018_mutant_lobeyness_collapse (P_hull A_cell k_rop A_lobe A_indent : Int)
    (hk : k_rop > 0) (hA : A_lobe > 0) :
    lobed_perimeter P_hull 0 A_lobe = P_hull ∧
    lobed_perimeter P_hull k_rop 0 = P_hull ∧
    lobed_hull_area A_cell 0 A_indent = A_cell ∧
    lobed_perimeter P_hull k_rop A_lobe > P_hull
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L = P_perim / P_hull = (P_hull + k_rop A_lobe) / P_hull,  S = A_cell / (A_cell + k_rop A_indent)  ⇒  L(k_rop=0) = 1, S(k_rop=0) = 1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.01.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-019-0500-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.32794> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled ROP2–ROP6 Cross-Inhibitory Cortical Reaction–Diffusion, Turgor-Driven Largest Empty Circle (LEC) Stress Scaling & Sinusoidal Anticlinal Wall Buckling" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.lobed_perimeter" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_039.sapala_2018_mutant_lobeyness_collapse" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "MorphoEval simulation-faithfulness rubric v0.1.0" ;
    dct:description "Weighted 0-100 rubric for the faithfulness of a morphology simulation to its organism and source model; Overall = weighted mean. Each score is a pk:LLMClaimAssessment (ProbKnow rubric-assessment template) of the pk:Claim pkr:claim/morphoeval-<sim> against one dimension (dct:subject the dimension concept, pk:assessmentType morphoeval/<version>/<dimension>) with pk:hasScore = score/100 — an uncalibrated rubric score, not a probability — and a pk:hasVerdict band; the overall score has the rubric itself as dct:subject and is also the pk:weightOfEvidence of the claim." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/rubric.yaml> ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> .

